<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="KR5c0126-en-82bf339c" type="comment"><teiHeader><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Comments to 莊子</title><editor role="creator">Ding Maoyuan 丁茂遠</editor></titleStmt><publicationStmt><ab>published electronically as part of the TLS project at https://hxwd.org</ab><availability status="2"><ab>This work has been licensed for use in the TLS</ab></availability></publicationStmt><sourceDesc><bibl><title/>2025</bibl><p>Comments and notes to <bibl corresp="#KR5c0126"><title xml:lang="och">莊子</title></bibl>for translation <ref target="#KR5c0126-en-79235b2b"/>.</p></sourceDesc></fileDesc><profileDesc><creation resp="#CH">Initially created: <date>2025-06-08T13:42:19.651+09:00</date> by CH</creation></profileDesc></teiHeader><text><body><div><head>Comments</head><p xml:id="KR5c0126-start"><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-20a.35" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-11-26T10:27:11.987+09:00">Test</seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:21:14.442+09:00">“Do you exist </seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:21:23.857+09:00">or do you not exist?” </seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:25:13.274+09:00">He got no answer, and could see no countenance there,</seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:24:40.67+09:00">just a darkness, an emptiness. </seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:22:11.062+09:00">Ceaselessly gazing after him, </seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:22:19.331+09:00">listening for him, </seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:22:42.617+09:00">groping for him, he could find nothing to see, nothing to hear, nothing to take hold of. </seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:22:54.522+09:00">Radiance said, </seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:23:00.8+09:00">“This is truly reaching it! </seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:23:11.224+09:00">But who can reach this? </seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:23:19.884+09:00">Nothingness can be present to me, </seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:23:43.249+09:00">but never yet the lack of nothingness, </seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-16a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:24:12.31+09:00">for once I have come to it, it becomes the lack only of being</seg><seg corresp="#KR5c0126_tls_022-17a.1" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-08-25T00:24:05.881+09:00">—so how, from where, could I come to reach it?”</seg></p></div></body></text></TEI>